comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T12:33:23.036Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched all 2,230 live items across every status for GH-844, local npm tarballs, npm pack, tgz package sources, archive extraction, traversal, and symlink safety. Closed pm-59gj owns the package-first baseline, closed pm-g072 owns dependency-spec injection safety, and closed pm-vnjh owns ecosystem smoke infrastructure; none accepts package archives. The open namespace consolidation pm-tnud is the canonical parent. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/844"
  "2026-08-03T07:39:29.247Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: real npm archives first failed through the public resolver, then passed safe install plus traversal/root/link/entry/expanded-byte bounds. The tar@7.5.22 API and ReadEntry types were verified from installed package declarations before implementation; no shell extraction is used for local archives."
  "2026-08-03T08:06:47.248Z","harness:codex","Evidence: full coverage gate passes 6,758 tests across 422 files at exactly 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines. Local archive coverage includes local and npm: source routing, no npm-pack execution, metadata fallbacks, entry/expanded/archive limits, links, device/path escapes, and required npm package layout."
  "2026-08-03T08:23:07.106Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance: fresh isolated Node and Bun workspaces installed the real @unbrained/pm-command-kit npm tarball from its original local archive path, activated it, and invoked command-kit echo under Bun. A separately packed pm-cli consumer ran the public SDK plus npx --no-install pm and bunx --no-install pm at 2026.8.3."
  "2026-08-03T09:06:50.397Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/880 carries the safe local npm archive implementation, tests, packed-consumer proof, and exact-head gates."
